    "title": "Much cooler air finally starts settling in - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Zack Webster ,\n11 hours ago SYNOPSIS – Six of the last seven days have featured a tied or broken record high in Dothan, and that streak will finally come to an end as we head through the second half of this week. The rain is gone, and skies will clear out a bit through the rest of our Wednesday morning. We’ll still turn warmer into the afternoon, but expect highs to run around 10 to 15 degrees cooler than where we’ve been for much of the past several days. Drier air really starts to take its hold over the region tonight, and temperatures are much cooler despite all of the sunshine that we’ll see for Thanksgiving and much of our Black Friday. We’ll turn a little warmer once again through the weekend, then rain chances are back on the increase by early next week. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
